# probe-dev.log — ExecApkProbe builder self-checks for cap_apk_probe.py

All runs are builder development self-checks in scratch
(/fast/scratch/hyaku/revenger-r100/ExecApkProbe); none is a scoring run and
none ran before FROZEN as a scored result (C2 target runs belong to the L1
after freeze). Genuine runs use the contract argv from the lane root:
`PYTHONUTF8=1 python3 -B reports/round-100/cap_apk_probe.py --fixture
corpus/fixtures/apk-r65 --work <scratch>`.

Environment: androguard 4.1.4 (~/.local/bin/androguard, `androguard --version`
-> "androguard, version 4.1.4"), apktool 3.0.3 (~/.local/bin/apktool,
`apktool --version` -> "3.0.3"), python3 3.14.8 (/usr/bin/python3). No tools
installed or upgraded this session.

## Dev history (bugs found and fixed before final bytes)

- Run A (initial): genuine tamper leg failed "pool pattern occurs 0 times" —
  pool_encoding() read the string-pool flags at pool+20 (stringsStart) instead
  of pool+16 (flags). Fixed; flags now read at manifest offset 8+16=24,
  UTF8_FLAG 0x100 detected.
- Run B: flipped-fixture control crashed the probe with an uncaught
  `zipfile.BadZipFile: Bad CRC-32 for file 'AndroidManifest.xml'` when
  tamper_leg() read the corrupt member (empty stdout, rc=1 from the traceback,
  contract lines lost). Fixed: zip reads in tamper_leg() guarded
  (BadZipFile/OSError/ValueError -> leg fail), and all contract lines now
  print incrementally as computed.
- Run C (L1-requested pre-freeze fix, sha bbd3b801… -> b2c9d189…): androguard
  writes `androguard.log` into its cwd, so decoder subprocesses now run with
  cwd=<probe scratch dir>. First attempt broke a relative --fixture (decoders
  resolved the APK against their new cwd: "File … does not exist"); fixed by
  resolving the fixture path to absolute in probe() (`Path(args.fixture).resolve()`).
  Verified lane cleanliness: `git -C <lane> status --porcelain` identical
  before/after the genuine lane-root run and after the whole battery; no
  androguard.log in the lane; scratch (with any androguard.log) removed on
  exit. The pre-existing lane-root androguard.log was left untouched.

